    "stop_reason": "success",
    "result_text": "The full suite is green: **263 tests, 0 failures, 0 errors**.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented `telephoneDisplay` as a derived, read-time response field \u2014 the human-formatted version of the stored E.164 `telephone`, while `telephone` itself stays raw E.164.\n\nThe response DTO (`OwnerDto`) is generated from `openapi.yml`, and all other derived read-time fields (`displayName`, `initials`, `locality`, `contactPreference`, etc.) are computed in `OwnerMapper`, so I followed that same pattern:\n\n1. **`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 added a `telephoneDisplay` read-only property to the `Owner` schema so the generated `OwnerDto` gains the getter/setter.\n\n2. **`src/main/java/.../mapper/OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 added `@Mapping(target = \"telephoneDisplay\", expression = \"java(telephoneDisplay(owner))\")` and a `telephoneDisplay(Owner)` method that:\n   - Splits the E.164 country code from the national digits using the same known-code list as `NormalizeOwnerTelephone` (`61`, then `1`, longest-first).\n   - Emits `+<cc>`, a single space, then the national digits grouped in threes from the left \u2014 e.g. `+61412345678` \u2192 `+61 412 345 678`.\n   - Returns the value unchanged if it isn't a recognizable E.164 string (defensive against seed/legacy data), and `null` for a null owner, matching the sibling derivations.\n\nThe raw `telephone` field is untouched, so it continues to return the stored E.164 value. The new `AcceptanceTest.coreFormatsTelephoneDisplay` passes (`telephone` = `+61412345678`, `telephoneDisplay` = `+61 412 345 678`), and no existing tests regressed.",
